## Outcome and conditions

Derive the OLS normal equations and centered solution, calculate fitted values/residuals, use matrix dimensions/full rank, and distinguish algebraic fitting identities from population assumptions.

Required components (all must be elicited and passed):

- C1: Derives both normal equations and centered formula with nonzero denominator.
- C2: Correct coefficients, fitted values, residual signs and units/domain.
- C3: Correct matrix dimensions/full-rank condition and joint interpretation.
- C4: Names six assumptions and distinguishes residual identities from exogeneity.

